; Refuse the line with "What ?"
;
; For a typed line (#R$75F1 gives Z) prints "What ?" in the input window and
; returns NZ to the caller of the parser, so the line is not executed. For an
; order being parsed (SAY TO) the error is ignored and the parser goes on with
; the next word at #R$75B4. #R$7924 enters here after dropping a return
; address. #R$792F is the second entry, which prints the message only (used when
; the parser ends with a sentence that is not finished).
; .
; Hardware: none directly (the message goes through #R$72DD).
;
; E Parser flags (kept for #R$75B4)
; O:F NZ when the line was refused (#R$792F)
@label=RejectLine
c$7929 CALL $75F1    ; TestTypedLine
 $792C JP NZ,$75B4   ; an order: ignore the error, ParseNextWord
; This entry point is used by the routines at #R$6C00 and #R$75F6.
@label=PrintWhat
*$792F LD HL,$AD9F   ; "What ?"
 $7932 LD A,$01      ;
 $7934 LD ($B701),A  ; RawOutputFlag: the input window
 $7937 CALL $72DD    ; PrintMessage
 $793A OR $01        ; NZ
 $793C RET           ;
